# Builder Performance

- Treat Builder interaction performance as a primary requirement.
- Analyze and identify the root cause before changing code.
- Limit each performance fix to the reported interaction and affected element.
- Preserve UI, behavior, layout structure, drag-and-drop semantics, and saved data.
- Do not optimize by removing required work or delaying it beyond the measured interaction.
- Avoid new render cascades, unstable references, broad Context subscriptions, and unnecessary store subscriptions.
- Prefer selectors, stable callbacks, refs for transient drag state, and scoped updates.
- Verify Hook dependencies semantically; never add or remove dependencies blindly.

# Performance Monitor Integrity

- Do not change Builder Performance Monitor thresholds to make results pass.
- Do not suppress, skip, or redefine valid samples without evidence of measurement error.
- Keep interaction labels, ownership, frame-gap, commit, render, and long-task measurements accurate.
- If the application is slow, fix application work rather than the monitor.
- If measurement is suspected, reproduce repeatedly and compare with browser performance tooling first.

# Verification

- Run targeted lint after edits and full lint before handoff.
- Run the production build.
- Re-test the same interaction 3–5 times.
- Report remaining warnings or uncertainty; stop for manual UI testing when requested.
